---
import ProductLayout from "../layouts/ProductLayout.astro";

const description = "Checkride's roadmap: what already works, and the work needed to make one isolated restore drill trustworthy end to end.";

const phases = [
  { title: "Define the drill", state: "Done", later: false, items: ["Versioned YAML drill contract", "Scenario templates and the interactive Studio", "Strict validation in the Go API"] },
  { title: "Evaluate recorded evidence", state: "Done, early", later: false, items: ["V0 to V4 verdicts with the first failed level", "Recovery time by phase, including unaccounted time", "Exact data loss from an acknowledged-write ledger", "Studio report review and export", "Signed evidence with local verification", "Prometheus metrics and a bundled Grafana dashboard"] },
  { title: "Run one isolated lab drill", state: "Done, lab only", later: false, items: ["Separate source and restore k3d clusters", "Delete the source namespace after backup", "Restore and verify one PostgreSQL write", "Record V0 to V3 checks and clean up namespaces"] },
  { title: "Harden execution and capture", state: "Next", later: true, items: ["Collect evidence from the system itself, with tamper evidence", "Application-specific V4 checks", "A repeatable CI lab gate that recovers from interruption", "More scenarios, and guidance for operating this safely"] },
];
---
<ProductLayout title="Roadmap" description={description} current="roadmap">
  <section class="page-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Make one drill trustworthy end to end</h1>
      <p class="lead">The next hard problem is not another dashboard. It is running one isolated PostgreSQL recovery safely, collecting the evidence from the system instead of from the runner's say-so, and cleaning up properly when something goes wrong.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="rows">
      {phases.map((phase) => (
        <div class="row">
          <h2>{phase.title}</h2>
          <ul>
            {phase.items.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
          </ul>
          <span class:list={["row-state", { later: phase.later }]}>{phase.state}</span>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="margin-top: 48px;">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Staying small on purpose</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Restore orchestration touches clusters, storage and application data, so the first version is deliberately narrow: one supported stack, one separate restore cluster, one scenario, a bounded run time and explicit cleanup.</p>
        <p>Nothing here involves production restores, production credentials or a public package release.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</ProductLayout>
